PREREQUISITES: 
The vNIC must already be added to the LPAR manually before
running this test. This script does NOT provision the vNIC itself.

input parameters:
interfaces ---> Interface name(s) of the existing vNIC on the system.
                Example: "eth1" or "eth1 eth2"
                (Alternatively, mac_id can also be provided).
mac_id ---> MAC address(es) of the vNIC interface (Optional if interfaces
            is provided). Example: "02:03:03:03:03:01"
device_ip ---> IP address to be configured on the vNIC interface after
               DLPAR.
netmasks ---> Netmask value for the vNIC interface.
               Example: "255.255.255.0"
peer_ip ---> Peer IP to ping after DLPAR to verify backend traffic.
num_of_dlpar ---> Number of DLPAR remove/add cycles to perform per
                  slot. Default: 1
lockdown_enable ---> Set to True to enable kernel lockdown before
                     running DLPAR (used in vnic_dlpar_secureboot.yaml).
                     Default: False
lockdown_mode ---> Kernel lockdown mode to activate when
                   lockdown_enable is True.
                   Accepted values: integrity, confidentiality
                   Default: integrity

YAML Files:
- vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml:
    Configuration for standard vNIC DLPAR test execution.
- vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar_secureboot.yaml:
    Configuration for vNIC DLPAR test execution under kernel lockdown
    (Secure Boot mode).

Example Usage:
- Regular vNIC DLPAR:
  avocado run vnic_dlpar.py -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar.yaml

- vNIC DLPAR under Kernel Lockdown / Secure Boot:
  avocado run vnic_dlpar.py -m vnic_dlpar.py.data/vnic_dlpar_secureboot.yaml
